{"name":"Port Wine","hex":"#6e0c0d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"port wine","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of fortified wine traditionally made in Portugal."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/port_wine"}],"entries":[{"title":"Port wine","blocks":[{"text":"Port wine, or simply port, is a Portuguese fortified wine produced in the Douro Valley of northern Portugal. It is typically a sweet red wine, often served with dessert, although it also comes in dry, semi-dry, and white varieties."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Port_wine.jpg/330px-Port_wine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Port_wine","wikidata":"Q191034"},{"title":"Port","blocks":[{"text":"A port is a maritime facility comprising one or more wharves or loading areas, where ships load and discharge cargo and passengers. Although usually situated on a sea coast or estuary, ports can also be found far inland, such as Hamburg, Manchester and Duluth; these access the sea via rivers or canals. Because of their roles as ports of entry for immigrants as well as soldiers in wartime, many port cities have experienced dramatic multi-ethnic and multicultural changes throughout their histories."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Manhattan.jpg/330px-Manhattan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Port","wikidata":"Q44782"},{"title":"Wine","blocks":[{"text":"Wine is an alcoholic drink made from fermented grape juice. It is produced and consumed in many regions around the world, in a wide variety of styles which are influenced by different varieties of grapes, growing environments, viticulture methods, and production techniques."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Red_and_white_wine_in_glass.jpg/330px-Red_and_white_wine_in_glass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wine","wikidata":"Q282"},{"title":"Wine red","blocks":[{"text":"The color wine, or wine red, also called bordeaux, vinous, or vinaceous, is a dark shade of red and brown. It is a representation of the typical color of red wine."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c0/Red_Wine_Glass.jpg/330px-Red_Wine_Glass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wine_red","wikidata":"Q3014419"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Bodega_Sandeman%2C_Vila_Nova_de_Gaia%2C_Portugal%2C_2012-05-09%2C_DD_06.JPG/500px-Bodega_Sandeman%2C_Vila_Nova_de_Gaia%2C_Portugal%2C_2012-05-09%2C_DD_06.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Bodega_Sandeman%2C_Vila_Nova_de_Gaia%2C_Portugal%2C_2012-05-09%2C_DD_06.JPG/1280px-Bodega_Sandeman%2C_Vila_Nova_de_Gaia%2C_Portugal%2C_2012-05-09%2C_DD_06.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Bodega_Sandeman%2C_Vila_Nova_de_Gaia%2C_Portugal%2C_2012-05-09%2C_DD_06.JPG/500px-Bodega_Sandeman%2C_Vila_Nova_de_Gaia%2C_Portugal%2C_2012-05-09%2C_DD_06.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sandeman cellar, Vila Nova de Gaia, Portugal","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABodega_Sandeman%2C_Vila_Nova_de_Gaia%2C_Portugal%2C_2012-05-09%2C_DD_06.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/VinhoDoPorto_Garantia.jpg/500px-VinhoDoPorto_Garantia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/VinhoDoPorto_Garantia.jpg/500px-VinhoDoPorto_Garantia.jpg?utm_source